{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1154351-do-gurahl-roll-to-remain-active","id":1154351,"title":"Do Gurahl roll to remain active?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-31T05:57:34-07:00","id":1154351,"title":"Do Gurahl roll to remain active?","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Hey!</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">In the W20 changing breeds book says Gurahl &quot;regenerate like Garou&quot;. It also says instead of using rage like garou do they pump strength/stamina and they can gain temporary health levels.<br /> <br /> In the W20 book, Remain active is described under the \u201cuse rage\u201d section (page 147). Then is mentioned again in the damage and health sections (page 245+).<br /> <br /> I know this is rules lawyering and background/logic are more important to interpret the rules than the actual wording.<br /> <br /> From a background point of view, it make sense to me the remain active role is limited to the Warriors of Gaia. The Gurahl can use rage to gain additional health levels instead of rolling to remain active. Then they pump strength/stamina instead of getting additional actions.<br /> <br /> Garous must be significantly better in combat than other changing breeds, don\u2019t they?</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11010,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","user":"erSito","date":". 10-31-2017, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T06:30:22-07:00","id":1154357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>erSito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1154351-do-gurahl-roll-to-remain-active#post1154351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Hey!</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">In the W20 changing breeds book says Gurahl &quot;regenerate like Garou&quot;. It also says instead of using rage like garou do they pump strength/stamina and they can gain temporary health levels.<br /> <br /> In the W20 book, Remain active is described under the \u201cuse rage\u201d section (page 147). Then is mentioned again in the damage and health sections (page 245+).<br /> <br /> I know this is rules lawyering and background/logic are more important to interpret the rules than the actual wording.<br /> <br /> From a background point of view, it make sense to me the remain active role is limited to the Warriors of Gaia. The Gurahl can use rage to gain additional health levels instead of rolling to remain active. Then they pump strength/stamina instead of getting additional actions.<br /> <br /> Garous must be significantly better in combat than other changing breeds, don\u2019t they?</span></span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pack tactics are a hell of a thing. They have numbers and organization that counts for alot vs other changing breeds. I would say if a CB &quot;regenerates like garou&quot; then yes they can remain active.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T09:53:13-07:00","id":1154420,"title":"","content":"As a default, apply the rules for werewolves to the other changing breeds unless stated otherwise (or blatantly stupid, I might add =P).<br /> It has been mentioned <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103867-w20-core-rules-adapted-by-cb20\"> here</a>.<br /> <br /> So yes, remaining active is a roll that should be granted to any fera using Rage (so, not the Nuwisha). Also, the greatest Rage benefit in combats are the extra actions and I definitely would not call the Gurhali a match for the Garou in combat. Sure, so you have double strength and a few extra stamina and health levels, but the Gets have more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}